================================================================================
packaging/artifacts/ -- the distributed Windows bundle
================================================================================

Nothing under packaging/artifacts/ is tracked in this repository; it is
produced by packaging/build_bundle.py and ignored by .gitignore. It is
recorded here because it is the only thing users receive, and it carries code
this repository does not contain.

Besides this project's MIT code, the bundle embeds:

  * CPython and its standard library      -- PSF License
  * this project's runtime dependencies   -- see README.md dependency table
  * PyInstaller's compiled bootloader and
    its PyInstaller/loader modules        -- GPL-2.0-or-later
                                             WITH Bootloader-exception
  * PyInstaller run-time hooks
    (PyInstaller/hooks/rthooks, and one
    from pyinstaller-hooks-contrib)       -- Apache-2.0

PyInstaller's COPYING.txt grants, under the heading "Bootloader Exception",
unlimited permission to link or embed the compiled bootloader and related
files into combinations with other programs and to distribute those
combinations "without any restriction coming from the use of those files";
its GPL terms continue to cover modification of those files and their
distribution when not linked into a combined executable. The run-time hooks
are separately licensed Apache-2.0 by the same file. Neither places this
project's own code under the GPL: Technocore Station remains MIT.

vendor/technocore-reference/ is NOT in the bundle. It is a test oracle only.

